# Signing keys never belong in the repository. The release key lives in GitHub Secrets; losing or
# leaking it means the app can never be updated again under this application id.
*.jks
*.keystore
debug.keystore

# The one exception: the debug key is deliberately committed. A debug key is not a secret —
# Android's own default debug key is public with the password "android" — and Play Store will not
# accept anything signed with it. Committing it is what makes debug APKs update each other across
# machines and CI runs instead of each build refusing to replace the last.
!keystore/fixhora-debug.jks
